==Opinion polls==
{{main|Opinion polling for the 2022 Colombian presidential election}}
===First round===
{{#section:Opinion polling for the 2022 Colombian presidential election|First Round Presidential polling chart}}

===Second round===
{{#section:Opinion polling for the 2022 Colombian presidential election|Second Round Presidential polling chart}}

The polls revealed both generational and professional cleavages. Voters were more likely to vote for Petro the younger they were. The majority of employees, unemployed and students were planning to vote for Petro, while the majority of the self-employed, housewives and pensioners were planning to vote for Hernandez. The wealthier voters were, the more likely they were to vote for Hernandez.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.lasillavacia.com/silla-nacional/las-grandes-diferencias-entre-los-votantes-de-petro-y-rodolfo/|title=Las grandes diferencias entre los votantes de Petro y Rodolfo|first=María José|last=Restrepo|date=14 June 2022|website=La Silla Vacía|accessdate=21 August 2024|archive-date=5 April 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240405203207/https://www.lasillavacia.com/silla-nacional/las-grandes-diferencias-entre-los-votantes-de-petro-y-rodolfo/|url-status=live}}</ref>

== Results ==
Shortly after the first round, the process of judicial scrutiny commenced. The process found an increase of 0.1% votes, reportedly the lowest in Colombian history and slightly altered the final results for the initial round.<ref>{{cite web |title=La diferencia entre el preconteo y el escrutinio municipal en la primera vuelta de las elecciones presidenciales de 2022 fue de tan solo el 0,1 % |url=https://www.registraduria.gov.co/La-diferencia-entre-el-preconteo-y-el-escrutinio-municipal-en-la-primera-vuelta.html |publisher=National Registry of Colombia |access-date=4 June 2022 |language=es |date=1 June 2022|archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20220607002815/https://www.registraduria.gov.co/La-diferencia-entre-el-preconteo-y-el-escrutinio-municipal-en-la-primera-vuelta.html|archive-date=7 June 2022|url-status=dead}}</ref> As none of the presidential nominees obtained at least 50% of the votes, a [[Two-round system|runoff]] was held on 19 June 2022, between the top two candidates, [[Gustavo Petro]] and [[Rodolfo Hernández Suárez]].<ref name=":0" /> Petro won the runoff, becoming the first [[left-wing]] candidate to be elected [[president of Colombia]] since the country's independence in 1810.<ref name=":1" /><ref name="The Dialogue 2022"/><ref name="Galindo 2022"/> The results for the second round saw the lowest record of blank votes in over 20 years. Furthermore, turnout for the run-off was 58.17%, the highest since [[1998 Colombian presidential election|1998]].<ref name=esr/>
