==Aftermath==
Hernández called Petro to congratulate him on his victory. He also encouraged Petro to remain committed to the "anti-corruption discourse". Hernández and Marelen Castillo also thanked Colombians that voted for them.<ref>{{cite news |title=Marelen Castillo thanks Rodolfo Hernández voters: "their votes have not been in vain" |url=https://www.infobae.com/america/colombia/2022/06/20/marelen-castillo-agradece-a-votantes-de-rodolfo-hernandez-sus-votos-no-han-sido-en-vano/ |access-date=20 June 2022 |work=Infobae |date=20 June 2022 |language=es |archive-date=20 June 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220620074316/https://www.infobae.com/america/colombia/2022/06/20/marelen-castillo-agradece-a-votantes-de-rodolfo-hernandez-sus-votos-no-han-sido-en-vano/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Castillo announced shortly after the election that she would accept a seat in the chamber of representatives reserved for the second-place vice presidential candidate. She also encouraged Hernández to take a senate seat, although he was still to decide.<ref>{{cite news |title="Seré opositora si no se le cumple al pueblo colombiano": Marelen Castillo irá a la Cámara |url=https://www.semana.com/nacion/articulo/sere-opositora-si-no-se-le-cumple-al-pueblo-colombiano-marelen-castillo-ira-a-la-camara/202218/ |access-date=20 June 2022 |work=Semana |date=20 June 2022 |archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20220815030826/https://www.semana.com/nacion/articulo/sere-opositora-si-no-se-le-cumple-al-pueblo-colombiano-marelen-castillo-ira-a-la-camara/202218/ |archive-date=15 August 2022|url-status=live|language=es}}</ref> On 23 June, Hernández announced that he would become a senator.<ref>{{cite news |title=¿Rodolfo Hernández renunciará al Senado para aspirar a la Gobernación de Santander? |url=https://www.semana.com/confidenciales/articulo/rodolfo-hernandez-renunciara-al-senado-para-aspirar-a-la-gobernacion-de-santander/202217/ |access-date=24 June 2022 |work=Semana |date=23 June 2022 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20220624114613/https://www.semana.com/confidenciales/articulo/rodolfo-hernandez-renunciara-al-senado-para-aspirar-a-la-gobernacion-de-santander/202217/ |archive-date=24 June 2022 |url-status=live|language=es}}</ref> President [[Iván Duque]] called Petro to congratulate him; he also pledged to carry out a smooth transition.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Pozzebon |first1=Stefano |title=Left-wing candidate and former guerrilla Gustavo Petro wins Colombian presidential race |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2022/06/17/americas/gustavo-petro-profile-intl-latam/index.html |access-date=22 June 2022 |work=CNN |date=20 June 2022|archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20220930114305/https://edition.cnn.com/2022/06/17/americas/gustavo-petro-profile-intl-latam/index.html|archive-date=30 September 2022|url-status=live|location=[[Bogotá]]}}</ref>

===International state reactions===
*{{flag|Argentina}}: President [[Alberto Fernández]] and Vice President [[Cristina Fernández de Kirchner]] both congratulated Petro and Márquez. President Fernández added that "[their] victory reafirms democracy and reasures the path toward a united Latin America".<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.infobae.com/politica/2022/06/19/alberto-fernandez-felicito-a-gustavo-petro-por-su-eleccion-como-presidente-de-colombia/|work=[[Infobae]]|title=Alberto Fernández y Cristina Kirchenr felicitaron a Gustavo Petro por su elección como presidente de Colombia|date=19 June 2022|access-date=20 June 2022|language=es|archive-date=19 June 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220619235352/https://www.infobae.com/politica/2022/06/19/alberto-fernandez-felicito-a-gustavo-petro-por-su-eleccion-como-presidente-de-colombia/|url-status=live}}</ref>
*{{flag|Brazil}}: President [[Jair Bolsonaro]] did not congratulate Petro following his victory and criticized a speech by Petro where he advocated for the release of detained protestors. Bolsonaro used the speech to criticize left-wing opponent [[Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva]], stating: "Did you see today's speech by the new president of Colombia? 'Release all the boys in prison, everyone'. Lula is going to release the little boys who killed someone for a cell phone to have a beer."<ref>{{Cite web |title=Bolsonaro compara Gustavo Petro a Lula – DW – 21/06/2022 |url=https://www.dw.com/pt-br/bolsonaro-compara-gustavo-petro-a-lula/a-62202066 |access-date=2022-06-21 |website=DW |language=pt |archive-date=21 June 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220621155051/https://www.dw.com/pt-br/bolsonaro-compara-gustavo-petro-a-lula/a-62202066 |url-status=live }}</ref>
*{{flag|Canada}}: Prime Minister [[Justin Trudeau]] congratulated Petro and Márquez, noting that the latter was "the first Afro-Colombian to take on the role". Trudeau also added that he is "looking forward to working with both on priorities like democracy, gender equality, and climate action".<ref>{{Cite tweet|last=Trudeau|first=Justin|user=JustinTrudeau|number=1538927579054350337|title=Congratulations to @PetroGustavo, the President-elect of Colombia; and to @FranciaMarquezM, the Vice President-elect and the first Afro-Colombian to take on the role. I'm looking forward to working with you both on priorities like democracy, gender equality, and climate action.}}</ref>
*{{flag|Chile}}: President [[Gabriel Boric]] congratulated Petro and called his victory "joy" for Latin America. Boric also congratulated Márquez and invited Petro to "work together for the unity of [Latin America] in a rapidly changing world."<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/presidente-boric-felicita-a-petro-y-a-marquez-por-vencer-en-las-elecciones-de-colombia/CWMUGT5HLNDCVKGRD7MVIOOO4M/|work=[[La Tercera]]|title=Presidente Boric felicita a Petro y a Márquez por vencer en las elecciones de Colombia|date=19 June 2022|access-date=20 June 2022|last=Martínez|first=Roberto|language=es|archive-date=20 June 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220620000858/https://www.latercera.com/politica/noticia/presidente-boric-felicita-a-petro-y-a-marquez-por-vencer-en-las-elecciones-de-colombia/CWMUGT5HLNDCVKGRD7MVIOOO4M/|url-status=live}}</ref>
*{{flag|China}}: President [[Xi Jinping]] sent a congratulatory message to Petro, stating that the relationship between Colombia and China is at "a new starting point," expressed his willingness to work with Petro to "deepen mutual political trust," "practical cooperation" and "work on the further development of bilateral relations." Petro, via his Twitter account "thanked the President of China for his words, assuring "a productive relationship between Colombia and China based on overcoming the climate crisis and building fair and decarbonised economies."<ref>{{cite news |title=Xi Jinping, presidente de China, envía mensaje a Gustavo Petro: "Será un punto de inicio de las relaciones bilaterales" |url=https://www.infobae.com/america/colombia/2022/06/27/xi-jinping-presidente-de-china-envia-mensaje-a-gustavo-petro-sera-un-punto-de-inicio-de-las-relaciones-bilaterales/ |access-date=27 June 2022 |work=Infobae |date = 27 June 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220627222354/https://www.infobae.com/america/colombia/2022/06/27/xi-jinping-presidente-de-china-envia-mensaje-a-gustavo-petro-sera-un-punto-de-inicio-de-las-relaciones-bilaterales/ |archive-date=27 June 2022 |url-status=live |language=es}}</ref><ref>{{Cite tweet|last=Petro|first=Gustavo|user=petrogustavo|number=1541632029414014976|title=Agradezco al presidente de China sus palabras y estoy seguro habrá una relación productiva entre Colombia y China basada en la superación de la crisis climática y la construcción de economías justas y descarbonizadas.}}</ref>
*{{flag|Costa Rica}}: President [[Rodrigo Chaves Robles]] posted on [[Twitter]], "congratulations to the President-elect of Colombia, Mr Gustavo Petro and his Vice-President Ms Francia Márquez, for [their] triumph, in a democratic and free process. Our best wishes to the Colombian people, with whom we wish a magnificent relationship."<ref>{{cite news |title=Mandatario de Costa Rica felicitó a presidente electo de Colombia |url=https://www.prensa-latina.cu/2022/06/19/mandatario-de-costa-rica-felicito-a-presidente-electo-de-colombia |access-date=23 June 2022 |work=Prensa Latina |date=19 June 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220621214829/https://www.prensa-latina.cu/2022/06/19/mandatario-de-costa-rica-felicito-a-presidente-electo-de-colombia |archive-date=21 June 2022 |url-status=live |language=es}}</ref>
*{{flag|Dominican Republic}}: President [[Luis Abinader]] congratulated Petro on Twitter and praised the "civility shown on this day that supports democracy" and credited the electoral authorities for ensuring the election was "organised and peaceful".<ref>{{cite news |last1=Arias |first1=Edili |title=Abinader felicita a Petro por su triunfo en las elecciones de Colombia |url=https://eldia.com.do/abinader-felicita-a-petro-por-su-triunfo-en-las-elecciones-de-colombia/ |access-date=23 June 2022 |work=El Día |date=20 June 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220620125252/https://eldia.com.do/abinader-felicita-a-petro-por-su-triunfo-en-las-elecciones-de-colombia/ |archive-date=20 June 2022|url-status=live |language=es}}</ref>
*{{flag|Cuba}}: President [[Miguel Díaz-Canel]] congratulated Petro and posted on Twitter, "I express my fraternal congratulations to Gustavo Petro on his election as President of Colombia in a historic popular victory". Díaz-Canel also expressed interest in expanding bilateral relations between Colombia and Cuba. The Cuban foreign minister, [[Bruno Rodríguez Parrilla]], also congratulated Petro. Rodríguez described the electoral triumph as a significant win for upholding peace in Colombia.<ref>{{cite news |title=El presidente de Cuba felicita a Petro por su triunfo electoral en Colombia |url=https://www.swissinfo.ch/spa/colombia-elecciones_el-presidente-de-cuba-felicita-a-petro-por-su-triunfo-electoral-en-colombia/47686976 |access-date=24 June 2022 |work=Swiss info |date=20 June 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220622143657/https://www.swissinfo.ch/spa/colombia-elecciones_el-presidente-de-cuba-felicita-a-petro-por-su-triunfo-electoral-en-colombia/47686976 |archive-date=22 June 2022 |location=[[Havana]] |url-status=live|language=es}}</ref>
*{{flag|Ecuador}}: President [[Guillermo Lasso]] called Petro to congratulate him. Lasso said he looked forward to strengthening "friendship...cooperation [and] development" between Colombia and Ecuador.<ref>{{cite news |title=Lasso felicita a Petro por ganar la Presidencia de Colombia |url=https://www.larepublica.ec/blog/2022/06/19/lasso-felicita-a-petro-por-ganar-la-presidencia-de-colombia/ |access-date=22 June 2022 |work=La República |date=19 June 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220621231735/https://www.larepublica.ec/blog/2022/06/19/lasso-felicita-a-petro-por-ganar-la-presidencia-de-colombia/ |archive-date=21 June 2022 |language=es}}</ref>
*{{flag|European Union}}: The [[High Representative of the Union for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy|High Representative for Foreign Affairs]] [[Josep Borrell]] congratulated Petro, saying that "Colombia is a key partner for the EU" and that the president-elect can "count on the European Union" to continue strengthening their partnership. He also added that the Colombian election was "a vote for political change and a more egalitarian and inclusive society".<ref name=universal>{{Cite news |title=Las felicitaciones y mensajes de líderes mundiales a Gustavo Petro |url=http://www.eluniversal.com.co/elecciones/2022/noticias/las-felicitaciones-y-mensajes-de-lideres-mundiales-gustavo-petro-626 |access-date=21 June 2022|work=El Universal|archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20220621232756/https://www.eluniversal.com.co/elecciones/2022/noticias/las-felicitaciones-y-mensajes-de-lideres-mundiales-gustavo-petro-626 |archive-date=21 June 2022|url-status=live|language=es}}</ref>
*{{flag|Haiti}}: Acting President [[Ariel Henry]] congratulated Petro and Márquez via Twitter and wrote, "I would like to extend my sincere congratulations to Mr Gustavo Petro on his victory in the presidential elections in Colombia. I wish you success, as well as your vice-president, Ms Francia Márquez."<ref name=universal/>
*{{flag|Honduras}}: President [[Xiomara Castro]] posted on Twitter, "On behalf of the people of Honduras, I congratulate the brave people of Colombia for choosing the historic social change represented today by President-elect Gustavo Petro."<ref>{{cite news |title=Xiomara Castro felicita al izquierdista Petro por ganar la Presidencia colombiana |url=https://www.efe.com/efe/america/politica/xiomara-castro-felicita-al-izquierdista-petro-por-ganar-la-presidencia-colombiana/20000035-4834805 |access-date=23 June 2022 |work=Agencia EFE |date=20 June 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220622011738/https://www.efe.com/efe/america/politica/xiomara-castro-felicita-al-izquierdista-petro-por-ganar-la-presidencia-colombiana/20000035-4834805 |archive-date=22 June 2022 |location=[[Tegucigalpa]] |url-status=live|language=es}}</ref>
*{{flag|Mexico}}: President [[Andrés Manuel López Obrador]] described Petro's victory as a "historic event" and that it bought about an end to a period of "domination." Obrador also characterised Petro's triumph as a win for the "progressive bloc".<ref>{{cite news |title=AMLO hails progressive advance in LatAm after Petro's win in Colombia |url=https://www.laprensalatina.com/amlo-hails-progressive-advance-in-latam-after-petros-win-in-colombia/ |access-date=20 June 2022 |work=La Prensa Latina |date=20 June 2022 |location=[[Mexico City]] |archive-date=20 June 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220620182020/https://www.laprensalatina.com/amlo-hails-progressive-advance-in-latam-after-petros-win-in-colombia/ |url-status=live }}</ref>
*{{flag|Panama}}: In a social media post, President [[Laurentino Cortizo]] stated, "On behalf of Panama, I congratulate the president-elect of Colombia, Gustavo Petro, on his arrival at the Casa de Nariño."<ref>{{cite news |title=Presidente de Panamá felicita a Gustavo Petro por su elección en Colombia |url=https://www.swissinfo.ch/spa/colombia-elecciones_presidente-de-panamá-felicita-a-gustavo-petro-por-su-elección-en-colombia/47686880 |access-date=22 June 2022 |work=SWI |date=19 June 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220621220818/https://www.swissinfo.ch/spa/colombia-elecciones_presidente-de-panamá-felicita-a-gustavo-petro-por-su-elección-en-colombia/47686880 |archive-date=21 June 2022 |url-status=live|language=es}}</ref>
*{{flag|Paraguay}}: President [[Mario Abdo Benítez]] congratulated Petro on Twitter, writing, "Our congratulations to Gustavo Petro as the new president-elect of the Republic of Colombia and to the brotherly Colombian people for this exemplary election day that reaffirms their democratic commitment."<ref name=universal/>
*{{flag|Peru}}: President [[Pedro Castillo]] said he spoke with Petro to congratulate him on his "historic democratic victory", adding that he and Petro are "united by a common feeling that seeks collective, social and regional integration improvements for our peoples"<ref>{{Cite news |date=2022-06-19 |title=Pedro Castillo saluda triunfo de Gustavo Petro en las elecciones presidenciales de Colombia Rodolfo Hernández RMMN {{!}} POLITICA |url=https://elcomercio.pe/politica/pedro-castillo-saluda-triunfo-de-gustavo-petro-en-las-elecciones-presidenciales-de-colombia-rodolfo-hernandez-rmmn-noticia/ |access-date=2022-06-21 |newspaper=El Comercio |language=es |archive-date=21 June 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220621160104/https://elcomercio.pe/politica/pedro-castillo-saluda-triunfo-de-gustavo-petro-en-las-elecciones-presidenciales-de-colombia-rodolfo-hernandez-rmmn-noticia/ |url-status=live }}</ref>
*{{flag|Sahrawi Arab Democratic Republic}}: President [[Brahim Ghali]] expressed his congratulations to Petro for his election. Ghali also stated that "His election and the actual development of the elections constitute further proof of the strength of Colombian democracy".<ref>{{Cite web |date=June 20, 2022 |title=El presidente de la República, Brahim Gali, felicita al electo presidente de la República de Colombia, Gustavo Petro |url=https://www.spsrasd.info/news/es/articles/2022/06/20/40260.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220620214640/https://www.spsrasd.info/news/es/articles/2022/06/20/40260.html |archive-date=June 20, 2022 |access-date=June 20, 2022 |website=Sahara Press Service |language=es}}</ref>
*{{flag|Spain}}: Prime Minister [[Pedro Sánchez]] expressed his "best wishes" for Petro and Márquez. He also assured, "We will continue to strengthen the ties that unite us".<ref name=universal/>
*{{flag|United States}}: Secretary of State [[Antony Blinken]] spoke with Petro to congratulate him on his election and discuss collaboration on issues such as "climate change, improv[ing] public health, and advanc[ing] inclusive economic opportunity". Blinken also noted "U.S. support for full implementation of Colombia's commitments under the [[Colombian peace process|2016 Peace Accord]]".<ref>{{Cite web |title=Secretary Blinken's Call with Colombian President-Elect Petro |url=https://www.state.gov/secretary-blinkens-call-with-colombian-president-elect-petro/ |access-date=2022-06-21 |website=United States Department of State |language=en |archive-date=21 June 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220621121541/https://www.state.gov/secretary-blinkens-call-with-colombian-president-elect-petro/ |url-status=live }}</ref> President [[Joe Biden]] also spoke with Petro to congratulate him. Biden noted that he "looks forward to working with the President-elect to continue strengthening bilateral cooperation, including on climate change, health security, and implementation of the 2016 Peace Accord" and discussed "bilateral security and counternarcotics cooperation". They also "agreed to have their teams follow up and engage directly on shared interests".<ref>{{Cite web |date=2022-06-21 |title=Readout of President Biden's Call with President-Elect Gustavo Petro of Colombia |url=https://bidenwhitehouse.archives.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/06/21/readout-of-president-bidens-call-with-president-elect-gustavo-petro-of-colombia/ |access-date=2022-06-21 |website=The White House |language=en-US |archive-date=21 June 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220621223259/https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/06/21/readout-of-president-bidens-call-with-president-elect-gustavo-petro-of-colombia/ |url-status=live }}</ref>
*{{flag|Uruguay}}: President [[Luis Lacalle Pou]] called Petro to congratulate him. The Uruguayan ministry of foreign affairs wished Petro "success in his future management" and applauded the "exemplary electoral process".<ref>{{cite news |title=El gobierno felicitó a Gustavo Petro por su victoria en las elecciones en Colombia |url=https://www.elobservador.com.uy/nota/el-gobierno-felicito-a-gustavo-petro-por-su-victoria-en-las-elecciones-en-colombia-2022620112642 |access-date=22 June 2022 |work=El Observador |date=20 June 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220620145820/https://www.elobservador.com.uy/nota/el-gobierno-felicito-a-gustavo-petro-por-su-victoria-en-las-elecciones-en-colombia-2022620112642 |archive-date=20 June 2022 |url-status=live|language=es}}</ref>
*{{flag|Venezuela}}: President [[Nicolás Maduro]] congratulated Petro on his victory, saying: "I congratulate Gustavo Petro and Francia Marquez, for the historic victory in the presidential elections in Colombia. The will of the Colombian people was heard, who came out to defend the path of democracy and peace. New times are on the horizon for this brother country."<ref name=":03">{{Cite web |date=2022-06-20 |title=¿Cuál ha sido la posición de Gustavo Petro sobre Venezuela? |url=https://www.elnacional.com/venezuela/cual-ha-sido-la-posicion-de-gustavo-petro-sobre-venezuela/ |access-date=2022-06-22 |website=[[El Nacional (Venezuela)|El Nacional]] |language=es |archive-date=22 June 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220622094243/https://www.elnacional.com/venezuela/cual-ha-sido-la-posicion-de-gustavo-petro-sobre-venezuela/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

=== Other international reactions ===
Peruvian writer, politician, and Nobel laureate [[Mario Vargas Llosa]] declared "[Colombians] voted wrong, let's see how Petro acts."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mateo |first=Juan José |date=2022-06-20 |title=Vargas Llosa, sobre las elecciones de Colombia: 'Han votado mal, a ver cómo actúa Petro' |url=https://elpais.com/america-colombia/elecciones-presidenciales/2022-06-20/vargas-llosa-sobre-las-elecciones-de-colombia-han-votado-mal-a-ver-como-actua-petro.html |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240525175427/https://elpais.com/america-colombia/elecciones-presidenciales/2022-06-20/vargas-llosa-sobre-las-elecciones-de-colombia-han-votado-mal-a-ver-como-actua-petro.html |archive-date=2024-05-25 |access-date=2022-06-21 |website=[[El País]] |language=es}}</ref> [[Ron DeSantis]], the Republican [[Governor of Florida]], denounced Petro as a "former narco-terrorist and a Marxist" whose victory is going to be "disastrous" for Colombia.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2022-06-20 |title=Gov. DeSantis says Colombia election shows Marxism, totalitarianism spreading |url=https://floridapolitics.com/archives/533787-colombia-desantis/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230928211732/https://floridapolitics.com/archives/533787-colombia-desantis/ |archive-date=2023-09-28 |access-date=2022-06-21 |website=[[Florida Politics]] |language=en-US}}</ref> In the United Kingdom, former [[Leader of the Labour Party (UK)|Leader of the Labour Party]], [[Jeremy Corbyn]], praised Petro's victory as proof of the "power of community organising to build a popular policy platform to heal the divisions of the past and bring about social justice".<ref>{{Cite web |date=2022-06-20 |title=Colombia election: Latin America leftist leaders praise Petro win |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2022/6/20/colombia-election-latin-america-leftist-leaders-praise-petro-win |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230930032254/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2022/6/20/colombia-election-latin-america-leftist-leaders-praise-petro-win |archive-date=2023-09-30 |access-date=2022-06-21 |website=Al Jazeera |language=en}}</ref>

